-- title:
--   Degree-one prime sums for fixed fields of Gal(L/ℚ)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field that is Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$. The theorem asserts the predicate [`FrobeniusDensity.DegOneAsymptotic`](def/FrobeniusDensity_DegOneAsymptotic.html#L33) for $L$, which unfolds as follows: for every subgroup $H$ of the Galois group $L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$, with fixed field $E = L^{H}$ viewed as an intermediate field of $L/\mathbb{Q}$, and every finite set $S_{0}$ of natural numbers, consider the coefficients $a(\ell)$ defined to be $0$ for $\ell \in S_{0}$ and otherwise [`FrobeniusDensity.degOneCount`](def/FrobeniusDensity_DegOneAsymptotic.html#L22) $E$ at $\ell$, that is: the number of primes $\mathfrak{q}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{E}$ lying over the ideal of $\mathbb{Z}$ generated by $\ell$ whose residue ring $\mathcal{O}_{E}/\mathfrak{q}$ has cardinality exactly $\ell$, when $\ell$ is prime, and $0$ when $\ell$ is not prime. Then two assertions hold: first, for every real $s > 1$ the family $\ell \mapsto a(\ell)\,\ell^{-s}$, indexed by all natural numbers $\ell$, is summable; second, the function $s \mapsto \sum_{\ell}' a(\ell)\,\ell^{-s} + \log(s-1)$ is $O(1)$ along the filter of right-hand neighbourhoods of $1$, i.e. as $s \to 1^{+}$ within $(1,\infty)$.
--
--   This is the analytic input to Frobenius's density theorem: the Dirichlet series of degree-one primes of each subfield $L^{H}$ behaves like $-\log(s-1) + O(1)$ at $s = 1^{+}$, uniformly in the sense that the bound is asserted for every subgroup $H$ and every finite excluded set of primes. It is consumed by [`FrobeniusDensity.statement`](thm.html#FrobeniusDensity.statement), where the orbit-counting half of the density argument is carried out, and by [`LanglandsTunnell.towerDirichletDensity_add_of_orderOf_eq_eight`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.towerDirichletDensity_add_of_orderOf_eq_eight).
